WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.300
Next, the things that can put a hole in your boat.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.325
Go down the table.

3
00:00:05.575 --> 00:00:09.175
A rock that does not cover is always above water.

4
00:00:09.425 --> 00:00:12.475
Its height is given above mean high water.

5
00:00:12.725 --> 00:00:17.825
A rock that covers and uncovers shows at low tide and hides at high tide.

6
00:00:18.075 --> 00:00:21.875
A rock awash sits right at the surface at chart datum.

7
00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:27.350
A sunken rock, marked with a cross, is always under water, and may be dangerous.

8
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:33.575
A wreck is drawn as a little hull if part of it shows, and as crossed lines if it’s submerged.

9
00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:36.725
O b s t n means an obstruction.

10
00:00:36.975 --> 00:00:38.875
And then the qualifiers.

11
00:00:39.125 --> 00:00:41.650
P A is position approximate.

12
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.350
P D is position doubtful.

13
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.950
E D is existence doubtful.

14
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.250
Rep means reported, but not confirmed.

15
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.900
So how do you treat a hazard marked existence doubtful?

16
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.600
As if it’s there.

17
00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.675
Every one of them is real until you’ve proved otherwise.
